Dear Vincent,

I hope all is well with you.

I am trying to use GGIR to process raw tri-axial accelerometery data captured using the GENEActiv Original at the wrist during exercise on a treadmill. I am also collecting  biomechanical data (mocap, forces, emg) to measure knee joint loading. The exercise is my participants are walking and running on an 'instrumented' treadmill at various different speeds.

My aim is to use cut points from the wrist-worn accelerometer to determine the intensity of activity during the run and then synchronise this data with knee joint loading.

To do this, I am trying to process my accelerometery data (approximately 10 minutes of data captured) using GGIR. However, GGIR doesn't seem to like the small file size i am using.

Is there a way I can get around this?

Also, is there a way to get which 'intensity zone' the participant was in according to time?

Best wishes,

Karl

